IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whsnt-claims`

-- Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text (reprint REPW025) before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL. Dates are `the calendar date` day month year.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- a claimant under the Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT)`

§§ `Short names`

`no injury` MEANS `there was no injury or illness`
`no exposure` MEANS `there was no such exposure`
`in-patient` MEANS `immediate treatment as an in-patient in a hospital (s 36(a))`
`IM` MEANS `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`
`Cat 1` MEANS `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)`
`Cat 2` MEANS `a Category 2 offence: failing a duty, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
`Cat 3` MEANS `a Category 3 offence: failing a duty (s 33)`
`Part 6 offence` MEANS `discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct (ss 104, 107, 108, 109)`
`other individual` MEANS `an individual, not as a business or undertaking or its officer`
`business or officer` MEANS `an individual conducting a business or undertaking, or an officer of one`
`company` MEANS `a body corporate`
`discrimination` MEANS `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
`coercion` MEANS `coercion or inducement under s 108`
`themselves` MEANS `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))`
`procured` MEANS `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another to do it (s 112(2)(b))`
`affected` MEANS `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))`
`INJ` MEANS `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`
`COMP` MEANS `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`
`REIN` MEANS `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`
`OTHER` MEANS `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
`YES START` MEANS `yes: I may apply to the Work Health Court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1))`
`TOO LATE` MEANS `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
`improvement notice` MEANS `an improvement notice (s 191, item 7)`
`prohibition notice` MEANS `a prohibition notice (s 195, item 9)`
`non-disturbance notice` MEANS `a non-disturbance notice (s 198, item 10)`
`forfeiture` MEANS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
`INTERNAL` MEANS `internal review by the regulator first (s 224), then the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(b))`
`STRAIGHT` MEANS `straight to the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(a))`
`NOT ELIGIBLE` MEANS `no review: I am not an eligible person (s 223)`
`any day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2000

§§ `ss 35 to 37 -- notifiable incident`

#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` TRUE `no injury` `no exposure` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `in-patient` `no exposure` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance (s 36(c))` `no exposure` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `in-patient` `no exposure` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `none of these` `no exposure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `no injury` `electric shock (s 37(e))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `no injury` `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `none of these` `something else` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` FALSE `no injury` `no exposure` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

